From bf63f6fd779040c0aad8daf254fae83eb36db3da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:15:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Agregar button clipped on mobile in item modal

The item modal sheet used `overflow:hidden` with a `88vh` max-height. On
phones this cut off the "Agregar" CTA with no way to scroll to it, since
`vh` is measured against the address-bar-hidden viewport and the card
extended under the browser toolbar. Items with longer descriptions (e.g.
Cheetos) overflowed first, which is why only some products were affected.

- Item modal sheet: overflow-y:auto instead of hidden
- Add `max-height:88dvh` alongside `88vh` so sizing uses the visible area
- Pin "Agregar" with position:sticky so it is always tappable
- Pin "Enviar orden" in the cart modal, also below the fold with 4+ items
- Shrink hero image and tighten spacing under `@media (max-height:720px)`
- viewport-fit=cover + env(safe-area-inset-bottom) for the home indicator

Verified headless at iPhone SE/14 (Safari and Chrome chrome heights),
Galaxy S8, landscape, tablet, and the 1080x1920 kiosk view.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E1AYUaS3HxSPKZF8bUmWAK
---
 public/index.html | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/public/index.html b/public/index.html
index a97f2af..e7eed11 100644
--- a/public/index.html
+++ b/public/index.html
